{"type":"app","meta":{"headers":{"x-nextjs-stale-time":"300","x-nextjs-prerender":"1","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T_/layout,_N_T_/services/layout,_N_T_/services/[slug]/layout,_N_T_/services/[slug]/[topic]/layout,_N_T_/services/[slug]/[topic]/page,_N_T_/services/managed-detection-response/mdr-service-levels"},"routeCache":{"key":"/route-cache/APP_PAGE/063a2b0a5783015dd47d2f57e3b891a758b18dad3917eba4c1d9dcafa3ccebae/$/services/managed-detection-response/mdr-service-levels","owner":{"kind":"APP_PAGE","sourceRoute":"/services/[slug]/[topic]/page"},"isFallback":false}},"html":"<!DOCTYPE html><!--g101YmPtGAR_Y376xJTed--><html lang=\"en\" class=\"no-js theme-dark __variable_12fc7c __variable_d46058 __variable_ae301a __variable_a3cc63\"><head><meta charSet=\"utf-8\"/><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\"/><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/_next/static/css/864ef3ae0e55d690.css\" data-precedence=\"next\"/><style data-precedence=\"default\" data-href=\"envenox-nav envenox-button envenox-footer envenox-services envenox-section envenox-badge\">\n.nav {\n  position: fixed;\n  inset-inline: 0;\n  top: 0;\n  z-index: 50;\n  height: var(--nav-h);\n  color: var(--fg);\n  background-color: transparent;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;\n  transition:\n    background-color var(--dur-scene) var(--ease-theme),\n    border-color var(--dur-scene) var(--ease-theme),\n    color var(--dur-scene) var(--ease-theme),\n    backdrop-filter var(--dur-scene) var(--ease-theme);\n}\n/* Scrolled: the spec's var(--bg) + blur(10px). Held at 92% so the blur does\n   real work — an opaque fill would make backdrop-filter a no-op. */\n.nav[data-scrolled='true'] {\n  background-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--bg) 92%, transparent);\n  backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n  border-bottom-color: var(--border);\n}\n\n.nav__bar {\n  position: relative;\n  height: var(--nav-h);\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: var(--s6);\n}\n\n.nav__brand {\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-size: var(--text-lg);\n  font-weight: 700;\n  letter-spacing: -0.03em;\n  color: var(--fg);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  flex: none;\n}\n\n/* ---- desktop menu ---- */\n.nav__desktop { display: none; }\n@media (min-width: 1024px) {\n  .nav__desktop { display: block; flex: 1 1 auto; }\n}\n.no-js .nav__desktop { display: none; }\n\n.nav__list { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s1); list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n\n.nav__trigger,\n.nav__toplink {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: var(--s1);\n  appearance: none;\n  background: none;\n  border: 0;\n  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);\n  padding: var(--s2) var(--s3);\n  min-height: 36px;\n  font-family: var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  line-height: 1;\n  color: var(--muted-strong);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out), background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.nav__trigger:hover,\n.nav__toplink:hover { color: var(--fg); background-color: var(--surface); }\n.nav__trigger[data-state='open'] { color: var(--fg); }\n.nav__trigger-chevron { transition: transform var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out); }\n.nav__trigger[data-state='open'] .nav__trigger-chevron { transform: rotate(180deg); }\n\n/* ---- the panel. forceMount keeps the links in the HTML. ----\n   640px is not arbitrary: scaleIn/scaleOut animate scale(0.9) from a\n   \"top center\" origin, so each horizontal edge travels width * 0.1 / 2. At\n   640px that is exactly 32px — the ceiling. A wider panel would animate\n   further than the vocabulary allows, so the panel is capped, and the featured\n   cell leads as a full-width row rather than a left column. */\n.nav__panel {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: calc(var(--nav-h) - var(--s2));\n  left: 0;\n  width: min(640px, calc(100vw - var(--gutter) * 2));\n  transform-origin: top center;\n  opacity: 0;\n  visibility: hidden;\n  pointer-events: none;\n  background-color: var(--bg);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  padding: var(--s6);\n  box-shadow: 0 1px 0 0 var(--border);\n}\n.nav__panel[data-state='open'] {\n  opacity: 1;\n  visibility: visible;\n  pointer-events: auto;\n  animation: scaleIn var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.nav__panel[data-state='closed'] { animation: scaleOut var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out); }\n\n.nav__panel-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--s4); grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }\n\n.nav__featured {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  background-color: var(--surface);\n  padding: var(--s4);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  color: var(--fg);\n  transition: background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.nav__featured:hover { background-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--surface) 86%, var(--fg) 14%); border-color: var(--border-strong); }\n.nav__featured-label {\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-size: var(--text-lg);\n  font-weight: 600;\n  letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);\n  line-height: 1.2;\n}\n.nav__featured-blurb { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.45; }\n\n.nav__links { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 2px; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n.nav__links--single { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n.nav__link {\n  display: block;\n  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);\n  padding: var(--s2) var(--s3);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  color: var(--fg);\n  transition: background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.nav__link:hover { background-color: var(--surface); }\n.nav__link-label { display: block; font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.3; }\n.nav__link-blurb { display: block; font-size: var(--text-xs); color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.4; margin-top: 2px; }\n\n.nav__panel-foot { margin-top: var(--s4); padding-top: var(--s4); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }\n.nav__panel-all { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted-strong); text-decoration: none; }\n.nav__panel-all:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n\n/* ---- actions ---- */\n.nav__actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s3); margin-left: auto; flex: none; }\n\n.nav__hotline {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  padding: var(--s1) var(--s3);\n  min-height: 44px;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  color: var(--fg);\n  transition: background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.nav__hotline:hover { background-color: var(--surface); border-color: var(--fg); }\n.nav__hotline-icon { flex: none; color: var(--muted-strong); }\n.nav__hotline-text { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px; line-height: 1.1; }\n.nav__hotline-kicker {\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: 0.08em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--muted);\n}\n.nav__hotline-number {\n  font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono), ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;\n  white-space: nowrap;\n}\n@media (min-width: 480px) {\n  .nav__hotline-number { font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n}\n\n/* ---- narrow-viewport fit ----\n   At 320px the bar has 288px of usable width, and brand + --s6 gap + hotline\n   + burger measured well past it. The overflow was INVISIBLE: .nav is fixed and\n   body is overflow-x: clip, so no scroll test catches it — the right-hand\n   actions, including the IR hotline, were simply clipped off the edge.\n\n   What gets sacrificed, in order: the bar gap, then the hotline's own padding,\n   then its icon. The NUMBER is the last thing to go and it never does. Someone\n   reaching for this link is mid-breach and needs the digits, not the glyph —\n   and the kicker stays too, because a bare number with no label is a worse\n   affordance than a slightly cramped one. */\n@media (max-width: 639px) {\n  .nav__bar { gap: var(--s3); }\n  .nav__actions { gap: var(--s2); min-width: 0; }\n  .nav__hotline { padding: var(--s1) var(--s2); gap: var(--s1); }\n}\n@media (max-width: 479px) {\n  .nav__hotline-icon { display: none; }\n  .nav__brand { font-size: var(--text-base); }\n}\n\n.nav__cta { display: none; }\n@media (min-width: 1024px) { .nav__cta { display: inline-flex; } }\n\n/* ---- mobile <details> menu: the real no-JS path ---- */\n.nav__mobile { position: static; }\n@media (min-width: 1024px) { .nav__mobile { display: none; } }\n.no-js .nav__mobile { display: block; }\n\n.nav__burger {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  width: 44px;\n  height: 44px;\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  color: var(--fg);\n  cursor: pointer;\n  list-style: none;\n  transition: background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.nav__burger::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }\n.nav__burger:hover { background-color: var(--surface); border-color: var(--fg); }\n.nav__burger-close { display: none; }\n.nav__mobile[open] .nav__burger-open { display: none; }\n.nav__mobile[open] .nav__burger-close { display: inline-flex; }\n\n.nav__sheet {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: var(--nav-h);\n  left: 0;\n  right: 0;\n  max-height: calc(100dvh - var(--nav-h));\n  overflow-y: auto;\n  overscroll-behavior: contain;\n  background-color: var(--bg);\n  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n  padding: var(--s6) var(--gutter) var(--s8);\n}\n.nav__sheet-group + .nav__sheet-group { margin-top: var(--s6); padding-top: var(--s6); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }\n.nav__sheet-heading {\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  margin: 0 0 var(--s3);\n}\n.nav__sheet-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 2px; }\n.nav__sheet-link {\n  display: block;\n  padding: var(--s3) 0;\n  min-height: 44px;\n  font-size: var(--text-base);\n  color: var(--fg);\n  text-decoration: none;\n}\n.nav__sheet-link:hover { color: var(--muted-strong); }\n.nav__sheet-blurb { display: block; font-size: var(--text-xs); color: var(--muted); margin-top: 2px; }\n.nav__sheet-cta { margin-top: var(--s8); display: grid; gap: var(--s3); }\n.nav__sheet-hotline {\n  font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono), ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  color: var(--fg);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  display: block;\n  padding: var(--s3) 0;\n}\n\n.btn {\n  --btn-bg: transparent;\n  --btn-bg-hover: transparent;\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: transparent;\n  --btn-border-hover: transparent;\n\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  border: 1px solid var(--btn-border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  color: var(--btn-fg);\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: -0.01em;\n  line-height: 1;\n  text-align: center;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  /* ONLY colour transitions. A transform here would break the house rule. */\n  transition:\n    background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.btn:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg-hover);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border-hover);\n  /* Falls back to the resting label colour, so no existing variant changes.\n     A variant whose hover fill moves far in lightness needs to move its label\n     too, or the hover state quietly fails contrast while the resting state\n     passes — which is the kind of thing an audit on static screenshots misses. */\n  color: var(--btn-fg-hover, var(--btn-fg));\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true'],\n.btn:disabled {\n  opacity: 0.45;\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true']:hover,\n.btn:disabled:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border);\n}\n\n/* ---- sizes. md and lg clear the 44x44 touch target. ---- */\n.btn--sm { min-height: 32px; padding-inline: var(--s3); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--md { min-height: 44px; min-width: 44px; padding-inline: var(--s4); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--lg { min-height: 52px; min-width: 52px; padding-inline: var(--s6); font-size: var(--text-base); }\n\n.btn--full { width: 100%; }\n\n/* ---- variants ---- */\n.btn--primary {\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent);\n  --btn-fg: var(--accent-fg);\n  --btn-bg-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent);\n  --btn-border-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n}\n.theme-light .btn--primary {\n  /* On paper, --accent is the DARK copper (#A04F1A) because it has to pass\n     4.5:1 as link TEXT. As a large filled surface that same value reads muddy\n     brown, which is not what the brand is. A fill has a different contrast\n     problem from text: the requirement is on the LABEL against the fill, and\n     ink on vibrant copper measures 6.9:1 — comfortably clear. So the fill gets\n     the real brand copper and the label goes dark. Links and the focus ring\n     keep --accent and stay legible. */\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-fg: var(--ink-900);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--accent-600);\n  --btn-fg-hover: var(--paper-50);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--accent-600);\n}\n.btn--secondary {\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--fg);\n}\n.btn--ghost {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--border);\n}\n.btn--ghost:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n.btn--danger-quiet {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--muted-strong);\n}\n.btn--danger-quiet:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n\n.btn__icon { display: inline-flex; flex: none; }\n\n.foot { background-color: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); }\n.foot__top { display: grid; gap: var(--s12); padding-block: var(--s20) var(--s12); }\n@media (min-width: 1024px) {\n  .foot__top { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 320px) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s16); }\n}\n\n.foot__brand { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s4); align-items: flex-start; }\n.foot__wordmark {\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-size: var(--text-2xl);\n  font-weight: 700;\n  letter-spacing: -0.03em;\n  color: var(--fg);\n  text-decoration: none;\n}\n.foot__positioning { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 46ch; margin: 0; }\n\n.foot__hotline {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: var(--s1);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  padding: var(--s4);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  color: var(--fg);\n  width: 100%;\n  transition: background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.foot__hotline:hover { background-color: var(--surface); border-color: var(--fg); }\n.foot__hotline-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s2); }\n.foot__hotline-number {\n  font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono), ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;\n  font-size: var(--text-lg);\n  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;\n  white-space: nowrap;\n}\n.foot__hotline-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-xs); line-height: 1.45; }\n\n.foot__cols { display: grid; gap: var(--s8); grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n@media (min-width: 768px) { .foot__cols { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--s6); } }\n.foot__col-heading {\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  margin: 0 0 var(--s3);\n}\n.foot__list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--s1); }\n.foot__link {\n  display: inline-block;\n  padding-block: var(--s1);\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  color: var(--muted-strong);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  transition: color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.foot__link:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n\n.foot__mid {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: var(--s8);\n  padding-block: var(--s12);\n  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);\n}\n@media (min-width: 768px) { .foot__mid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s16); } }\n\n.foot__offices { display: grid; gap: var(--s6); }\n@media (min-width: 480px) { .foot__offices { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }\n.foot__office-city {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  color: var(--fg);\n  margin: 0 0 var(--s1);\n}\n.foot__office-line { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; font-style: normal; }\n\n.foot__form { display: grid; gap: var(--s3); max-width: 44ch; }\n.foot__form-label {\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  color: var(--fg);\n}\n.foot__form-hint { font-size: var(--text-xs); color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }\n.foot__form-row { display: flex; gap: var(--s2); flex-wrap: wrap; }\n.foot__input {\n  flex: 1 1 14rem;\n  min-width: 0;\n  min-height: 44px;\n  background-color: var(--surface);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  padding: 0 var(--s3);\n  color: var(--fg);\n  font-family: inherit;\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  transition: border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out), background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.foot__input::placeholder { color: var(--muted); }\n.foot__input:hover { border-color: var(--fg); }\n.foot__submit {\n  min-height: 44px;\n  padding-inline: var(--s4);\n  border: 1px solid var(--accent);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  background-color: var(--accent);\n  color: var(--accent-fg);\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.foot__submit:hover {\n  background-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n  border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n}\n\n.foot__bottom {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: var(--s6);\n  padding-block: var(--s8);\n  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);\n}\n@media (min-width: 1024px) {\n  .foot__bottom { flex-direction: row; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--s12); }\n}\n.foot__legal { display: grid; gap: var(--s2); }\n.foot__legal-line { font-size: var(--text-xs); color: var(--muted); margin: 0; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 62ch; }\n.foot__legal-nav { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s1) var(--s4); list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n.foot__legal-link {\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  color: var(--muted);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  padding-block: var(--s1);\n  transition: color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.foot__legal-link:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n\n.foot__social { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s2); list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n.foot__social-link {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  min-height: 44px;\n  padding-inline: var(--s3);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  color: var(--muted-strong);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  transition: color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out), background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.foot__social-link:hover { color: var(--fg); background-color: var(--surface); border-color: var(--border-strong); }\n\n/* Announced, not shown — these links open in a new tab. */\n.foot__vh {\n  position: absolute;\n  width: 1px;\n  height: 1px;\n  padding: 0;\n  margin: -1px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  clip-path: inset(50%);\n  white-space: nowrap;\n  border: 0;\n}\n\n/* ---------- page-level type ---------- */\n.sv-h1 {\n  font-size: clamp(2rem, 6.4vw, 3.75rem);\n  margin: 0;\n  max-width: 20ch;\n}\n.sv-h1--long { max-width: 24ch; font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 5.6vw, 3rem); }\n.sv-sub {\n  margin: var(--s4) 0 0;\n  font-size: var(--text-lg);\n  color: var(--muted-strong);\n  max-width: 54ch;\n}\n.sv-lede {\n  margin: var(--s6) 0 0;\n  color: var(--muted-strong);\n  max-width: 68ch;\n}\n.sv-h2 {\n  font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.6vw, 2.25rem);\n  margin: 0;\n  max-width: 24ch;\n}\n.sv-h3 {\n  font-size: var(--text-xl);\n  margin: 0;\n}\n.sv-note {\n  margin: var(--s3) 0 0;\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  color: var(--muted);\n  max-width: 68ch;\n}\n\n/* ---------- section head ---------- */\n.sv-head { margin-bottom: var(--s12); }\n.sv-head__rule { height: 1px; background-color: var(--border); margin-bottom: var(--s6); }\n.sv-head__eyebrow { margin: 0 0 var(--s3); }\n.sv-head__lede { margin: var(--s4) 0 0; color: var(--muted-strong); max-width: 68ch; }\n\n/* ---------- hero ---------- */\n.sv-hero__eyebrow { margin: 0 0 var(--s4); }\n.sv-hero__actions {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: var(--s3);\n  margin-top: var(--s8);\n}\n.sv-hero__meta {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  gap: var(--s2) var(--s6);\n  margin: var(--s6) 0 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  list-style: none;\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  color: var(--muted);\n}\n\n/* ---------- credibility stat (first paragraph, PART 8.3) ---------- */\n.sv-cred {\n  margin: var(--s8) 0 0;\n  padding: var(--s6);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  background-color: var(--surface);\n  max-width: 68ch;\n}\n.sv-cred__figure {\n  display: block;\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-size: var(--text-2xl);\n  font-weight: 600;\n  letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);\n  line-height: var(--leading-snug);\n  color: var(--fg);\n}\n.sv-cred__context { display: block; margin-top: var(--s2); color: var(--muted-strong); }\n\n/* ---------- grids ---------- */\n.sv-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--s6); list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n@media (min-width: 680px) { .sv-grid--2 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }\n@media (min-width: 680px) { .sv-grid--3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }\n@media (min-width: 1000px) { .sv-grid--3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }\n.sv-grid > li { min-width: 0; }\n\n/* Two columns of prose: the heading rail and the body. */\n.sv-rail { display: grid; gap: var(--s8); }\n@media (min-width: 900px) {\n  .sv-rail { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 12fr); gap: var(--s16); }\n}\n.sv-rail__aside { min-width: 0; }\n.sv-rail__body { min-width: 0; }\n\n/* ---------- jump nav ---------- */\n.sv-jump {\n  position: sticky;\n  top: var(--nav-h);\n  z-index: 20;\n  background-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--bg) 94%, transparent);\n  backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n}\n.sv-jump__inner {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: var(--s1);\n  overflow-x: auto;\n  scrollbar-width: thin;\n  padding-block: var(--s2);\n  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;\n}\n.sv-jump__link {\n  flex: none;\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  min-height: 40px;\n  padding-inline: var(--s3);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  color: var(--muted-strong);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  white-space: nowrap;\n  transition: color var(--dur-micro) var(--ease-out), background-color var(--dur-micro) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.sv-jump__link:hover { color: var(--fg); background-color: var(--surface); }\n\n/* ---------- service card ---------- */\n.sv-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100%; gap: var(--s4); }\n.sv-card__top { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--s3); }\n.sv-card__icon { flex: none; color: var(--accent); margin-top: 2px; }\n.sv-card__name { font-size: var(--text-lg); margin: 0; }\n.sv-card__line { margin: 0; color: var(--muted-strong); }\n.sv-card__list {\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  list-style: none;\n  display: grid;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  color: var(--muted);\n}\n.sv-card__list li { display: flex; gap: var(--s2); }\n.sv-card__tick { flex: none; margin-top: 3px; color: var(--accent); }\n.sv-card__cta {\n  margin: auto 0 0;\n  padding-top: var(--s4);\n  font-size: var(--text-sm);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  color: var(--muted-strong);\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n}\n\n/* ---------- plain link list ---------- */\n.sv-links { display: grid; gap: 0; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }\n.sv-links > li { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }\n.sv-links__a {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;\n  align-items: baseline;\n  gap: var(--s4);\n  padding: var(--s4) 0;\n  min-height: 44px;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  color: var(--fg);\n  transition: color var(--dur-micro) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.sv-links__a:hover { color: var(--accent); }\n.sv-links__label { font-weight: 500; }\n.sv-links__blurb { display: block; margin-top: var(--s1); font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; }\n.sv-links__arrow { flex: none; color: var(--muted); align-self: center; }\n\n/* ---------- numbered methodology ---------- */\n.sv-phases { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; counter-reset: none; }\n.sv-phase {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  padding: var(--s6) 0;\n  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);\n}\n@media (min-width: 760px) {\n  .sv-phase { grid-template-columns: 3.5rem minmax(0, 14rem) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s6); align-items: start; }\n}\n.sv-phase__n { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted); }\n.sv-phase__name { font-size: var(--text-lg); margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; font-weight: 500; }\n.sv-phase__when { display: block; margin-top: var(--s1); font-size: var(--text-xs); color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; }\n.sv-phase__body { margin: 0; color: var(--muted-strong); }\n\n/* ---------- console exhibits ----------\n   One stacked band per placement. The gap is large on purpose: two dense\n   consoles with 24px between them read as one confused screenshot. */\n.sv-consoles { display: grid; gap: var(--s24); }\n\n/* ---------- phase card stack ----------\n   The stack primitive manages the sticky behaviour; this only sets the rhythm\n   above it and the two type roles inside a card. */\n.sv-phaseStack { margin-top: var(--s16); }\n.sv-phaseWhen {\n  margin: 0 0 var(--s3);\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  letter-spacing: 0.08em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--accent);\n}\n.sv-phaseBody { margin: 0; color: var(--muted-strong); line-height: var(--leading-normal); }\n\n/* The artefact stack sits under the deliverables heading in the rail aside.\n   Capped so it never outgrows a 7fr column on a wide viewport. */\n.sv-deliverableArt { margin-top: var(--s8); max-width: 30rem; }\n\n/* ---------- deliverables / outcomes ---------- */\n.sv-ticks { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--s4); }\n.sv-ticks > li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s3); color: var(--muted-strong); }\n.sv-ticks__mark { flex: none; margin-top: 4px; color: var(--accent); }\n\n/* ---------- chips (frameworks, stack, certifications) ---------- */\n.sv-chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s2); list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n/*\n * Local override, not an edit to Badge.tsx. Badge sets white-space: nowrap,\n * which is right for a severity word (\"Critical\") and wrong for \"AWS\n * Well-Architected Security Pillar\" inside a 288px content box: a nowrap item\n * cannot shrink, so flex-wrap does not save it and the layout blows out at\n * 320px. Measured in headless Chromium at 320px, which is how the two real\n * offenders on this tree were found.\n *\n * Scoped to the five containers in which these routes render a Badge, so it\n * can never reach a severity badge elsewhere on the site — those live in the\n * product UI and must stay on one line.\n */\n.sv-chips .badge,\n.sv-card .badge,\n.sv-note .badge,\n.sv-seam__cta .badge,\n.sv-hero__meta .badge { white-space: normal; text-align: left; }\n\n/* ---------- accreditation strip ---------- */\n.sv-accred { display: grid; gap: var(--s4); list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n@media (min-width: 680px) { .sv-accred { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }\n@media (min-width: 1000px) { .sv-accred { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }\n.sv-accred__item {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);\n  gap: var(--s3);\n  padding: var(--s4);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  min-width: 0;\n}\n.sv-accred__icon { flex: none; margin-top: 2px; color: var(--accent); }\n.sv-accred__label { font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: 500; color: var(--fg); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }\n.sv-accred__issuer { display: block; margin-top: var(--s1); font-size: var(--text-xs); color: var(--muted); }\n\n/* ---------- expert ---------- */\n.sv-expert { display: grid; gap: var(--s6); }\n@media (min-width: 760px) { .sv-expert { grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s8); } }\n.sv-expert__name { margin: 0; font-size: var(--text-xl); }\n.sv-expert__role { margin: var(--s1) 0 0; color: var(--accent); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.sv-expert__bio { margin: var(--s4) 0 0; color: var(--muted-strong); max-width: 60ch; }\n.sv-expert__certs-label { margin: var(--s6) 0 var(--s2); }\n\n/* ---------- case study ---------- */\n.sv-metrics { display: grid; gap: var(--s6); list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n@media (min-width: 680px) { .sv-metrics { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--s8); } }\n.sv-metric__value {\n  display: block;\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-size: var(--text-2xl);\n  font-weight: 600;\n  letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);\n  line-height: var(--leading-snug);\n  overflow-wrap: anywhere;\n}\n.sv-metric__label { display: block; margin-top: var(--s2); color: var(--muted-strong); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.sv-metric__note { display: block; margin-top: var(--s1); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-xs); }\n\n.sv-quote { margin: 0; }\n.sv-quote__text {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: var(--text-lg);\n  line-height: var(--leading-snug);\n  color: var(--fg);\n  max-width: 52ch;\n}\n.sv-quote__by { display: block; margin-top: var(--s4); font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted); font-style: normal; }\n.sv-quote__mark { color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: var(--s3); }\n\n/* ---------- definition grid (timeline / team / engagement) ---------- */\n.sv-defs { margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 0; }\n.sv-def { padding: var(--s6) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); display: grid; gap: var(--s2); }\n@media (min-width: 760px) { .sv-def { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 12rem) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s6); } }\n.sv-def__term { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted); margin: 0; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; }\n.sv-def__desc { margin: 0; color: var(--muted-strong); }\n\n/* ---------- the seam ---------- */\n.sv-seam { display: grid; gap: var(--s6); align-items: stretch; }\n@media (min-width: 980px) {\n  .sv-seam { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.12fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s4); align-items: stretch; }\n}\n.sv-seam__col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s4); height: 100%; }\n.sv-seam__centre { border-color: var(--accent); }\n.sv-seam__kicker { margin: 0 0 var(--s3); }\n.sv-seam__name { margin: 0; font-size: var(--text-xl); }\n.sv-seam__line { margin: var(--s3) 0 0; color: var(--muted-strong); }\n.sv-seam__body { margin: var(--s4) 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.sv-seam__cta { margin: auto 0 0; padding-top: var(--s6); }\n\n/* ---------- contrast pair (engagement models) ---------- */\n.sv-contrast { display: grid; gap: var(--s6); }\n@media (min-width: 900px) { .sv-contrast { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--s8); } }\n.sv-contrast__head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s3); margin-bottom: var(--s4); }\n.sv-contrast__icon { flex: none; color: var(--accent); }\n.sv-contrast__h { margin: 0; font-size: var(--text-lg); }\n.sv-contrast__rows { margin: 0; display: grid; }\n.sv-contrast__row { padding: var(--s4) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }\n.sv-contrast__term { margin: 0; font-size: var(--text-xs); letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }\n.sv-contrast__desc { margin: var(--s2) 0 0; color: var(--muted-strong); }\n\n/* ---------- form ---------- */\n.sv-form { display: grid; gap: var(--s6); max-width: 44rem; }\n.sv-field { display: grid; gap: var(--s2); min-width: 0; }\n.sv-field--check { grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: start; column-gap: var(--s3); }\n.sv-label { font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: 500; color: var(--fg); }\n.sv-req { color: var(--accent); margin-left: 2px; }\n.sv-help { font-size: var(--text-xs); color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }\n.sv-input,\n.sv-select,\n.sv-textarea {\n  width: 100%;\n  min-width: 0;\n  min-height: 44px;\n  padding: var(--s3) var(--s4);\n  background-color: var(--bg);\n  color: var(--fg);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  font: inherit;\n  font-size: var(--text-base);\n  transition: border-color var(--dur-micro) var(--ease-out), background-color var(--dur-micro) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.sv-textarea { min-height: 7.5rem; resize: vertical; line-height: var(--leading-normal); }\n.sv-input:hover, .sv-select:hover, .sv-textarea:hover { border-color: var(--fg); }\n.sv-input::placeholder, .sv-textarea::placeholder { color: var(--muted); }\n.sv-check { width: 20px; height: 20px; margin: 2px 0 0; accent-color: var(--accent); flex: none; }\n.sv-form__actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s4); align-items: center; }\n.sv-form__sla { margin: 0; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted); }\n/*\n * VALIDATION SUMMARY — revealed by :target, so it needs neither JavaScript nor\n * a searchParams read on the page.\n *\n * Reading ?enquiry= would have been the obvious way to show this, and it was\n * the first implementation. It is wrong: a page that reads searchParams opts\n * out of static generation, which would have made all sixteen service pages\n * dynamically rendered to display a message a visitor almost never sees. The\n * server action redirects to #enquiry-incomplete or #enquiry-email instead;\n * the browser scrolls to the matching block and :target reveals it. Static\n * generation survives, and so does the message.\n *\n * The common case never reaches here at all: the \"required\" attribute is\n * native constraint validation, which browsers enforce with scripting off.\n * The server check exists for a crafted POST, not a forgotten field.\n *\n * No --signal-* colour: Badge.tsx states severity colour is the one place in\n * the codebase those tokens appear, and a form error is not a severity rating.\n */\n.sv-form__error {\n  display: none;\n  padding: var(--s4);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);\n  border-left: 2px solid var(--fg);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  background-color: var(--surface);\n  scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--s8));\n}\n.sv-form__error:target { display: block; }\n.sv-form__error p { margin: 0; color: var(--fg); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n\n/*\n * A box that declares its own palette inside a band of another palette.\n * <Card> sets `color: inherit`, so a bare theme-* class on it would re-colour\n * the surface and leave the text behind; this sets both. Used on\n * /services/engagement-models, where the security retainer and the delivery\n * retainer sit side by side in the palette of their own act — the commercial\n * contrast made visible rather than described.\n */\n.sv-theme-box {\n  background-color: var(--bg);\n  color: var(--fg);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  padding: var(--s8);\n  min-width: 0;\n}\n\n/* ---------- misc ---------- */\n.sv-cta-band { display: grid; gap: var(--s6); }\n@media (min-width: 900px) { .sv-cta-band { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; align-items: center; gap: var(--s12); } }\n.sv-cta-band__actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s3); }\n\n.sv-hotline {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: var(--s4);\n  padding: var(--s8);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  background-color: var(--surface);\n}\n.sv-hotline__num {\n  font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono), ui-monospace, monospace;\n  font-size: clamp(1.375rem, 4.5vw, 1.75rem);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  color: var(--fg);\n  text-decoration: none;\n  overflow-wrap: anywhere;\n  transition: color var(--dur-micro) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.sv-hotline__num:hover { color: var(--accent); }\n\n.sv-stub {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: var(--s4);\n  padding: var(--s8);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  background-color: var(--surface);\n  max-width: 44rem;\n}\n.sv-prose-measure { max-width: 68ch; }\n.sv-sr {\n  position: absolute;\n  width: 1px; height: 1px;\n  padding: 0; margin: -1px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  clip: rect(0 0 0 0);\n  white-space: nowrap;\n  border: 0;\n}\n\n.sec {\n  position: relative;\n  background-color: var(--bg);\n  color: var(--fg);\n}\n/* Grain sits at z-index 1 with pointer-events none; content rides above it. */\n.sec > .u-container,\n.sec > .sec__bleed { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\n\n.badge {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  border: 1px solid var(--badge-border, var(--border));\n  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);\n  background-color: var(--badge-bg, transparent);\n  color: var(--badge-fg, var(--muted-strong));\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: 0.04em;\n  line-height: 1;\n  padding: var(--s1) var(--s2);\n  /* normal + balance, NOT nowrap. Three separate pages overflowed 320px because\n     a badge held arbitrary data — \"3 weeks review, 14 weeks remediation\",\n     \"AWS Solutions Architect Professional\", a credibility sentence — and an\n     unbreakable chip wider than its card pushes the whole grid track past the\n     viewport. A badge is a label primitive, but callers legitimately put\n     variable-length data in one, and the component should survive that rather\n     than require every caller to override it. Severity badges keep nowrap\n     below: \"Critical\" is two syllables and must never break. */\n  white-space: normal;\n  text-wrap: balance;\n}\n.badge--severity {\n  white-space: nowrap;\n}\n.badge--sm { font-size: var(--text-xs); padding: 2px var(--s2); }\n.badge--md { padding: var(--s1) var(--s3); }\n\n.badge--neutral {\n  --badge-bg: var(--surface);\n  --badge-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --badge-border: var(--border);\n}\n.badge--brand {\n  --badge-bg: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 12%, transparent);\n  --badge-fg: var(--accent);\n  --badge-border: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 38%, transparent);\n}\n\n/* --- the only --signal-* usage in the codebase --- */\n.badge--severity {\n  --badge-bg: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sig) 14%, transparent);\n  --badge-fg: var(--sig);\n  --badge-border: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sig) 42%, transparent);\n  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;\n}\n.badge--severity .badge__dot {\n  width: 6px;\n  height: 6px;\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  background-color: var(--sig);\n  flex: none;\n}\n.badge--critical { --sig: var(--signal-critical); }\n.badge--high { --sig: var(--signal-high); }\n.badge--medium { --sig: var(--signal-medium); }\n.badge--low { --sig: var(--signal-low); }\n.badge--info { --sig: var(--signal-info); }\n</style><link rel=\"preload\" as=\"script\" fetchPriority=\"low\" href=\"/_next/static/chunks/webpack-750339dbcd53e266.js\"/><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/4bd1b696-f785427dddbba9fb.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/1255-b84741b894bb9354.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/main-app-37618e55b880a2de.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/2619-3c9e02e22d10480a.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/4938-ec7db2048e7be43e.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/9393-bd02566ba347fb8d.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/app/layout-2f5ee25261e09e61.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/app/error-77708acc479f8cb3.js\" async=\"\"></script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/app/services/%5Bslug%5D/%5Btopic%5D/page-183f779d163f2d1b.js\" async=\"\"></script><meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#0a0d13\"/><title>What an MDR service level should commit to · Envenox</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"Every provider quotes 15 minutes. Fifteen minutes to what? An explainer under Managed Detection &amp; Response.\"/><meta name=\"application-name\" content=\"Envenox\"/><link rel=\"author\" href=\"https://envenox.com\"/><meta name=\"author\" content=\"Envenox Ltd\"/><meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"penetration testing,application security,managed detection and response,secure software development,custom software development,ISO 27001,SOC 2,DORA,NIS2\"/><meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\"/><meta name=\"creator\" content=\"Envenox Ltd\"/><meta name=\"publisher\" content=\"Envenox Ltd\"/><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, follow\"/><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://envenox.com/services/managed-detection-response/mdr-service-levels\"/><meta name=\"format-detection\" content=\"telephone=no, address=no, email=no\"/><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"What an MDR service level should commit to · Envenox\"/><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Every provider quotes 15 minutes. Fifteen minutes to what? An explainer under Managed Detection &amp; Response.\"/><meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://envenox.com/services/managed-detection-response/mdr-service-levels\"/><meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Envenox\"/><meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_GB\"/><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\"/><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\"/><meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"What an MDR service level should commit to · Envenox\"/><meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Every provider quotes 15 minutes. Fifteen minutes to what? An explainer under Managed Detection &amp; Response.\"/><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/icon.svg?0887ae5654435afa\" type=\"image/svg+xml\" sizes=\"any\"/><script>document.documentElement.classList.remove('no-js')</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https://envenox.com/#organization\",\"name\":\"Envenox\",\"legalName\":\"Envenox Ltd\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com\",\"description\":\"Envenox is a software development firm. We design, build and hand over the systems a business runs on — custom software, web applications, ERP, CRM, and the cloud platforms underneath them. What makes the work defensible is that we keep an offensive security practice on staff: our penetration testers read the code our engineers are writing and file findings into the same sprint backlog, so a system arrives already attacked rather than waiting for its first external test. That practice also works on its own, for clients who never buy a line of code from us. We work with regulated organisations across finance, healthcare, logistics and public sector, and we publish our own security posture at /trust.\",\"slogan\":\"We build the software. Then we try to break it.\",\"email\":\"hello@envenox.com\",\"telephone\":\"+44 20 4525 9101\",\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/envenox\",\"https://github.com/envenox\",\"https://x.com/envenox\"],\"address\":[{\"@type\":\"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"1 Fore Street Avenue, London EC2Y 9DT\",\"addressLocality\":\"London\",\"addressCountry\":\"United Kingdom\"},{\"@type\":\"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Level 7, Bay’s Galleria, Gulshan 1, Dhaka 1212\",\"addressLocality\":\"Dhaka\",\"addressCountry\":\"Bangladesh\"}],\"contactPoint\":[{\"@type\":\"ContactPoint\",\"contactType\":\"emergency\",\"name\":\"Incident response hotline\",\"telephone\":\"+44 20 4525 9100\",\"availableLanguage\":[\"en\"],\"hoursAvailable\":{\"@type\":\"OpeningHoursSpecification\",\"dayOfWeek\":[\"Monday\",\"Tuesday\",\"Wednesday\",\"Thursday\",\"Friday\",\"Saturday\",\"Sunday\"],\"opens\":\"00:00\",\"closes\":\"23:59\"}},{\"@type\":\"ContactPoint\",\"contactType\":\"sales\",\"email\":\"hello@envenox.com\",\"telephone\":\"+44 20 4525 9101\",\"availableLanguage\":[\"en\"]},{\"@type\":\"ContactPoint\",\"contactType\":\"security\",\"email\":\"security@envenox.com\",\"availableLanguage\":[\"en\"]}]},{\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"@id\":\"https://envenox.com/#website\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com\",\"name\":\"Envenox\",\"description\":\"Envenox is a software development firm. We ship production systems — custom software, web applications, ERP and the platforms underneath them — and we keep an offensive security practice on staff that attacks what we build before anyone else gets the chance.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-GB\",\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://envenox.com/#organization\"}}]}</script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/polyfills-42372ed130431b0a.js\" noModule=\"\"></script></head><body><div hidden=\"\"><!--$--><!--/$--></div><a class=\"u-skip\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a><header class=\"nav theme-dark transition-theme no-print\" data-scrolled=\"false\" data-nav-theme=\"dark\"><div class=\"nav__bar u-container\"><a class=\"nav__brand\" href=\"/\">Envenox</a><nav aria-label=\"Primary\" data-orientation=\"horizontal\" dir=\"ltr\" class=\"nav__desktop\"><div style=\"position:relative\"><ul data-orientation=\"horizontal\" class=\"nav__list\" dir=\"ltr\"><li><button id=\"radix-_R_klb_-trigger-Services\" data-state=\"closed\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"radix-_R_klb_-content-Services\" class=\"nav__trigger\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\">Services<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.625\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down nav__trigger-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></button><div id=\"radix-_R_klb_-content-Services\" aria-labelledby=\"radix-_R_klb_-trigger-Services\" data-orientation=\"horizontal\" data-state=\"closed\" class=\"nav__panel\" style=\"pointer-events:none\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"nav__panel-grid\"><a class=\"nav__featured\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/services/devsecops\"><span class=\"u-eyebrow\">Start here</span><span class=\"nav__featured-label\">Secure SDLC</span><span class=\"nav__featured-blurb\">The page that explains why one firm does both. Start here.</span></a><ul class=\"nav__links\"><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/services/cybersecurity\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Cybersecurity</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">Testing, assurance, detection and response</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/services/software-development\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Software Development</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">Product build, platform and modernisation</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/services/penetration-testing\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Penetration Testing</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">Web, mobile, network, cloud, API</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/services/application-security\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Application Security</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">Secure code review and SDLC uplift</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/services/managed-detection-response\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Managed Detection &amp; Response</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">24/7 SOC on your telemetry</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/services/grc-compliance\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">GRC &amp; Compliance</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">SOC 2, ISO 27001, PCI DSS, DORA, NIS2</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/services/custom-software\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Custom Software</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">Systems built to survive an audit</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/services/engagement-models\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Engagement Models</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">How retainers and projects actually run</span></a></li></ul></div><div class=\"nav__panel-foot\"><a class=\"nav__panel-all\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/services\">All <!-- -->services<!-- --> →</a></div></div></li><li><button id=\"radix-_R_klb_-trigger-Industries\" data-state=\"closed\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"radix-_R_klb_-content-Industries\" class=\"nav__trigger\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\">Industries<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.625\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down nav__trigger-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></button><div id=\"radix-_R_klb_-content-Industries\" aria-labelledby=\"radix-_R_klb_-trigger-Industries\" data-orientation=\"horizontal\" data-state=\"closed\" class=\"nav__panel\" style=\"pointer-events:none\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"nav__panel-grid\"><ul class=\"nav__links\"><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/industries/financial-services\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Financial Services</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/industries/healthcare\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Healthcare</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/industries/saas\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">SaaS &amp; Technology</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/industries/logistics\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Logistics</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/industries/public-sector\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Public Sector</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/industries/retail\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Retail &amp; Payments</span></a></li></ul></div><div class=\"nav__panel-foot\"><a class=\"nav__panel-all\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/industries\">All <!-- -->industries<!-- --> →</a></div></div></li><li><button id=\"radix-_R_klb_-trigger-Proof\" data-state=\"closed\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"radix-_R_klb_-content-Proof\" class=\"nav__trigger\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\">Proof<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.625\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down nav__trigger-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></button><div id=\"radix-_R_klb_-content-Proof\" aria-labelledby=\"radix-_R_klb_-trigger-Proof\" data-orientation=\"horizontal\" data-state=\"closed\" class=\"nav__panel\" style=\"pointer-events:none\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"nav__panel-grid\"><a class=\"nav__featured\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/sample-report\"><span class=\"u-eyebrow\">Start here</span><span class=\"nav__featured-label\">Anatomy of a report</span><span class=\"nav__featured-blurb\">Walk a real deliverable, redacted. See what actually lands in your inbox.</span></a><ul class=\"nav__links\"><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/case-studies\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Case Studies</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">24 stories, filterable</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/customers\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Customers</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">Who we work with, and what they say</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/certifications\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Certifications</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">Ours, with certificate numbers</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/trust\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Trust Centre</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">Our own security posture, published</span></a></li></ul></div></div></li><li><button id=\"radix-_R_klb_-trigger-Resources\" data-state=\"closed\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"radix-_R_klb_-content-Resources\" class=\"nav__trigger\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\">Resources<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.625\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down nav__trigger-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></button><div id=\"radix-_R_klb_-content-Resources\" aria-labelledby=\"radix-_R_klb_-trigger-Resources\" data-orientation=\"horizontal\" data-state=\"closed\" class=\"nav__panel\" style=\"pointer-events:none\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"nav__panel-grid\"><ul class=\"nav__links\"><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/resources\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">All resources</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/blog\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Insights</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/research\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Research &amp; Labs</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/tools\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Open-source tools</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/methodologies\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Methodologies</span></a></li></ul></div></div></li><li><button id=\"radix-_R_klb_-trigger-Company\" data-state=\"closed\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"radix-_R_klb_-content-Company\" class=\"nav__trigger\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\">Company<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.625\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down nav__trigger-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></button><div id=\"radix-_R_klb_-content-Company\" aria-labelledby=\"radix-_R_klb_-trigger-Company\" data-orientation=\"horizontal\" data-state=\"closed\" class=\"nav__panel\" style=\"pointer-events:none\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"nav__panel-grid\"><ul class=\"nav__links\"><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/about\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">About</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/about/leadership\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Leadership</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/approach\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">The Adversary Loop</span><span class=\"nav__link-blurb\">How we actually work</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/careers\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Careers</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__link\" data-radix-collection-item=\"\" href=\"/newsroom\"><span class=\"nav__link-label\">Newsroom</span></a></li></ul></div></div></li></ul></div></nav><div class=\"nav__actions\"><a class=\"nav__hotline\" href=\"tel:+442045259100\" data-ir-hotline=\"nav\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-phone nav__hotline-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M13.832 16.568a1 1 0 0 0 1.213-.303l.355-.465A2 2 0 0 1 17 15h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v3a2 2 0 0 1-2 2A18 18 0 0 1 2 4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v3a2 2 0 0 1-.8 1.6l-.468.351a1 1 0 0 0-.292 1.233 14 14 0 0 0 6.392 6.384\"></path></svg><span class=\"nav__hotline-text\"><span class=\"nav__hotline-kicker\">Breach? 24/7</span><span class=\"nav__hotline-number\">+44 20 4525 9100</span></span></a><a class=\"btn btn--primary btn--sm nav__cta\" href=\"/contact\"><span>Start a conversation</span></a><details class=\"nav__mobile\"><summary class=\"nav__burger\" aria-label=\"Navigation menu\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-menu nav__burger-open\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 5h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 12h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 19h16\"></path></svg><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-x nav__burger-close\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M18 6 6 18\"></path><path d=\"m6 6 12 12\"></path></svg></summary><nav class=\"nav__sheet\" aria-label=\"All pages\"><div class=\"nav__sheet-group\"><p class=\"nav__sheet-heading\">Services</p><ul class=\"nav__sheet-list\"><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/services/devsecops\">Secure SDLC<span class=\"nav__sheet-blurb\">The page that explains why one firm does both. Start here.</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/services/cybersecurity\">Cybersecurity</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/services/software-development\">Software Development</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/services/penetration-testing\">Penetration Testing</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/services/application-security\">Application Security</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/services/managed-detection-response\">Managed Detection &amp; Response</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/services/grc-compliance\">GRC &amp; Compliance</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/services/custom-software\">Custom Software</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/services/engagement-models\">Engagement Models</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/services\">All <!-- -->services</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"nav__sheet-group\"><p class=\"nav__sheet-heading\">Industries</p><ul class=\"nav__sheet-list\"><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/industries/financial-services\">Financial Services</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/industries/healthcare\">Healthcare</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/industries/saas\">SaaS &amp; Technology</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/industries/logistics\">Logistics</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/industries/public-sector\">Public Sector</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/industries/retail\">Retail &amp; Payments</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/industries\">All <!-- -->industries</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"nav__sheet-group\"><p class=\"nav__sheet-heading\">Proof</p><ul class=\"nav__sheet-list\"><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/sample-report\">Anatomy of a report<span class=\"nav__sheet-blurb\">Walk a real deliverable, redacted. See what actually lands in your inbox.</span></a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/case-studies\">Case Studies</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/customers\">Customers</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/certifications\">Certifications</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/trust\">Trust Centre</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"nav__sheet-group\"><p class=\"nav__sheet-heading\">Resources</p><ul class=\"nav__sheet-list\"><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/resources\">All resources</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/blog\">Insights</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/research\">Research &amp; Labs</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/tools\">Open-source tools</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/methodologies\">Methodologies</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"nav__sheet-group\"><p class=\"nav__sheet-heading\">Company</p><ul class=\"nav__sheet-list\"><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/about\">About</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/about/leadership\">Leadership</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/approach\">The Adversary Loop</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/careers\">Careers</a></li><li><a class=\"nav__sheet-link\" href=\"/newsroom\">Newsroom</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"nav__sheet-cta\"><a class=\"btn btn--primary btn--md btn--full\" href=\"/contact\"><span>Start a conversation</span></a><a class=\"nav__sheet-hotline\" href=\"tel:+442045259100\">Incident response, 24/7 — <!-- -->+44 20 4525 9100</a></div></nav></details></div></div></header><main id=\"main\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Envenox\",\"item\":\"https://envenox.com/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Services\",\"item\":\"https://envenox.com/services\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Cybersecurity\",\"item\":\"https://envenox.com/services/cybersecurity\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":4,\"name\":\"Managed Detection & Response\",\"item\":\"https://envenox.com/services/managed-detection-response\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":5,\"name\":\"What an MDR service level should commit to\",\"item\":\"https://envenox.com/services/managed-detection-response/mdr-service-levels\"}]}</script><section class=\"sec theme-dark transition-theme u-section grain\" data-theme-section=\"dark\" style=\"padding-top:calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--s16))\" aria-labelledby=\"topic-h1\"><div class=\"u-container\"><p class=\"u-eyebrow sv-hero__eyebrow\"><a class=\"u-link\" href=\"/services\">Services</a> · <a class=\"u-link\" href=\"/services/managed-detection-response\">Managed Detection &amp; Response</a></p><h1 id=\"topic-h1\" class=\"sv-h1 sv-h1--long\">Every provider quotes 15 minutes. Fifteen minutes to what?</h1><p class=\"sv-sub\">What an MDR service level should commit to</p><div class=\"sv-stub\" style=\"margin-top:var(--s8)\"><p style=\"margin:0\"><span class=\"badge badge--md badge--neutral\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-circle-alert\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"></circle><line x1=\"12\" x2=\"12\" y1=\"8\" y2=\"12\"></line><line x1=\"12\" x2=\"12.01\" y1=\"16\" y2=\"16\"></line></svg>Being written</span></p><p style=\"margin:0;color:var(--muted-strong)\">This explainer is being written. We would rather leave the page honest than fill it, so there is nothing here yet beyond the question itself.</p><p style=\"margin:0;color:var(--muted-strong)\">In the meantime the answer is in the Managed Detection &amp; Response page — or ask it directly on a scoping call and you will get it from the person who would lead the work.</p><div class=\"sv-hero__actions\" style=\"margin-top:0\"><a class=\"btn btn--primary btn--md\" href=\"/services/managed-detection-response\"><span>Back to Managed Detection &amp; Response</span><span class=\"btn__icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></span></a><a class=\"btn btn--secondary btn--md\" href=\"/contact\"><span>Start a conversation</span></a></div></div></div></section><section class=\"sec theme-deep transition-theme u-section\" data-theme-section=\"deep\" aria-labelledby=\"topic-parent\"><div class=\"u-container\"><div class=\"sv-head\"><div class=\"sv-head__rule\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><p class=\"u-eyebrow sv-head__eyebrow\">The service this sits under</p><h2 id=\"topic-parent\" class=\"sv-h2\">Managed Detection &amp; Response</h2><p class=\"sv-head__lede\">Analysts who read your architecture before they read your alerts.</p></div><p class=\"sv-prose-measure\" style=\"color:var(--muted-strong)\">Most managed detection is alert triage performed by people who have never seen your architecture diagram. They forward the alert, you do the investigation, and the service level is measured on how fast the forwarding happened. We run it differently. Onboarding starts with your architecture, your identity model and your crown-jewel systems, and the detections we write are specific to them — not a vendor rule pack with the noisy ones disabled. When something fires, an analyst investigates before you hear about it, and what reaches you is a conclusion with evidence and a recommended action, not a notification. Where you have authorised containment, we contain first and tell you immediately.</p><div class=\"sv-hero__actions\"><a class=\"btn btn--secondary btn--md\" href=\"/services/managed-detection-response\"><span>Read Managed Detection &amp; Response in full</span><span class=\"btn__icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></span></a></div></div></section><section class=\"sec theme-dark transition-theme u-section-tight\" data-theme-section=\"dark\" aria-labelledby=\"topic-siblings\"><div class=\"u-container\"><div class=\"sv-head\"><div class=\"sv-head__rule\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><p class=\"u-eyebrow sv-head__eyebrow\">Other questions</p><h2 id=\"topic-siblings\" class=\"sv-h2\">More on MDR</h2></div><ul class=\"sv-links\" aria-label=\"Other explainers under this service\"><li><a class=\"sv-links__a\" href=\"/services/managed-detection-response/build-or-buy-a-soc\"><span class=\"sv-links__label\">Build or buy a SOC<span class=\"sv-links__blurb\">At what size does running our own start to make sense?</span></span><svg class=\"sv-links__arrow\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></a></li></ul></div></section><section class=\"sec theme-deep transition-theme u-section-tight\" data-theme-section=\"deep\"><div class=\"u-container\"><div class=\"sv-cta-band\"><div><h2 class=\"sv-h2\">Analysts who read your architecture before they read your alerts.</h2><p class=\"sv-lede\">Annual retainer priced by log volume and endpoint count, with incident response hours included.</p></div><div class=\"sv-cta-band__actions\"><a class=\"btn btn--primary btn--lg\" href=\"/contact\"><span>Start a conversation</span></a><a class=\"btn btn--secondary btn--lg\" href=\"/services/managed-detection-response\"><span>Back to Managed Detection &amp; Response</span></a></div></div></div></section><!--$--><!--/$--></main><footer class=\"foot theme-dark transition-theme grain\" data-theme-section=\"dark\"><div class=\"u-container\"><div class=\"foot__top\"><div class=\"foot__brand\"><a class=\"foot__wordmark\" href=\"/\">Envenox</a><p class=\"foot__positioning\">Envenox is a software development firm. We ship production systems — custom software, web applications, ERP and the platforms underneath them — and we keep an offensive security practice on staff that attacks what we build before anyone else gets the chance.</p><a class=\"foot__hotline\" href=\"tel:+442045259100\" data-ir-hotline=\"footer\"><span class=\"foot__hotline-row\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-phone\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M13.832 16.568a1 1 0 0 0 1.213-.303l.355-.465A2 2 0 0 1 17 15h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v3a2 2 0 0 1-2 2A18 18 0 0 1 2 4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v3a2 2 0 0 1-.8 1.6l-.468.351a1 1 0 0 0-.292 1.233 14 14 0 0 0 6.392 6.384\"></path></svg><span class=\"u-eyebrow\">Incident response — 24/7</span></span><span class=\"foot__hotline-number\">+44 20 4525 9100</span><span class=\"foot__hotline-note\">Answered by a responder, 24/7. Median pickup under 4 minutes.</span></a></div><nav class=\"foot__cols\" aria-label=\"Footer\"><div><h2 class=\"foot__col-heading\">Cybersecurity</h2><ul class=\"foot__list\"><li><a class=\"foot__link\" href=\"/services/penetration-testing\">Penetration Testing</a></li><li><a class=\"foot__link\" href=\"/services/application-security\">Application Security</a></li><li><a class=\"foot__link\" href=\"/services/cloud-security\">Cloud Security</a></li><li><a class=\"foot__link\" href=\"/services/red-teaming\">Red Teaming</a></li><li><a class=\"foot__link\" href=\"/services/managed-detection-response\">Managed Detection &amp; Response</a></li><li><a class=\"foot__link\" href=\"/services/incident-response\">Incident Response</a></li><li><a class=\"foot__link\" href=\"/services/grc-compliance\">GRC &amp; Compliance</a></li><li><a class=\"foot__link\" href=\"/services/vciso\">vCISO</a></li></ul></div><div><h2 class=\"foot__col-heading\">Software Development</h2><ul class=\"foot__list\"><li><a class=\"foot_