\"Analysts who read your architecture before they read your alerts.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-prose-measure\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"var(--muted-strong)\"},\"children\":\"Most managed detection is alert triage performed by people who have never seen your architecture diagram. They forward the alert, you do the investigation, and the service level is measured on how fast the forwarding happened. We run it differently. Onboarding starts with your architecture, your identity model and your crown-jewel systems, and the detections we write are specific to them — not a vendor rule pack with the noisy ones disabled. When something fires, an analyst investigates before you hear about it, and what reaches you is a conclusion with evidence and a recommended action, not a notification. Where you have authorised containment, we contain first and tell you immediately.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-hero__actions\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-button\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"$35\"}],\"$L36\"]}]]}]}]]\n2c:[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-section\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"\\n.sec {\\n  position: relative;\\n  background-color: var(--bg);\\n  color: var(--fg);\\n}\\n/* Grain sits at z-index 1 with pointer-events none; content rides above it. */\\n.sec > .u-container,\\n.sec > .sec__bleed { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"sec theme-dark transition-theme u-section-tight\",\"data-theme-section\":\"dark\",\"style\":\"$undefined\",\"aria-labelledby\":\"topic-siblings\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"u-container\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-head\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-head__rule\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"u-eyebrow sv-head__eyebrow\",\"children\":\"Other questions\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"topic-siblings\",\"classN